# After ds41cardexp (a pick's two passes on the grouped GEMM), price BLOOMERY_PREFILL_GROUP=1 against the default 2.
# Decomposition [derived, ds41cardexp report section 2, from the v31cardtime and v31nsys forms]: at group 1 every
# layer-batch is a pick (~77 % of the slots on the card); the card was 55.1 ms/lb of which the tile path was 24.8;
# at GEMM speed ~35 ms/lb (rough). Host at group 1: union 19.5 + enqueue ~11 ms/lb. So group 1 is card-bound near
# ~35 ms/lb x 220 = ~7.7 s against group 2's measured ~9.5 s call: up to +20 %; if the card estimate is 25 % low
# (~44 ms/lb) the gain falls to ~+3 %.
# Resource timeline per lb: group 2 = host 41.5 (wall) over card ~32; group 1 = card ~35..44 (wall) over host ~30.
kind: ab
question: once the pick runs on the GEMM, does one batch a layer (group 1) beat two (group 2) on the 1017 prompt?
term: pp tok/s @ P = 4096, prose, depth 0, DeepSeek-V4.1-Flash-1017 Q3_K_M, --place a, A6000 - (group 1 - group 2) /
  group 2, same binary, paired by round
unit: %
predict: +3..+20
rounds: 4
condition: one lease, this tree's generate_ds41 alone, BLOOMERY_AB_ROUNDS=4 just depth-gpu-ds41
  prose:4096@BLOOMERY_STEP_STATS=1 prose:4096@BLOOMERY_STEP_STATS=1,BLOOMERY_PREFILL_GROUP=1, order rotated every
  round; both arms' plans name the same residency word and card_experts; no row carries [cpu-busy] or [other-busy]
decide-in: flip the group default to 1 for V4.1 at place a (the levers registry row's default), with this sitting
  as its evidence; then re-run the depth table's prose:512 row before the flip lands
decide-below: read card_in/card_out per lb: if the card stays above ~44 ms/lb, the GEMM pick did not reach group 1's
  shape or the copies serialize; keep group 2
decide-above: the host at group 1 was over-counted; re-derive the union from the stat prefill split line
